// VanguardMod human_base.hit — Pass 1+2 retune (2026-04-28)
//
// Geometry retuned based on measured bone distances from
// docs/notes/bone_distance_dump_2026-04-28.txt (body.mdx,
// 53 bones), captured during Phase 6.1.3 Pass 0 diagnosis.
//
// Live-test of v0.3.3 showed ~10% real-hit-rate for body
// shots; the bone-dump revealed two structural issues:
//
//   - GUT: Spine ↔ Spine1 (parent_dist 0.431 Quake-units)
//     was practically a 2D plane in the Z direction. Now
//     using Pelvis ↔ Spine2 — chained distance ≈10.53
//     Quake-units (Pelvis→Spine 4.876 + Spine→Spine1 0.431
//     + Spine1→Spine2 5.222), covering the lower torso.
//
//   - CHEST: Spine2 ↔ Spine3 (5.083 units) was a thin slice.
//     Now Spine1 ↔ Neck — chained distance ≈16.58 units
//     (5.222 + 5.083 + 6.274), spanning most of the upper
//     torso. Intentional overlap with GUT around Spine1-2
//     gives redundant coverage of the chest/belly boundary.
//
//   - GROIN: pelvis sphere widened from radius 5 → 7 to
//     cover the hip / lower-pelvis area more reliably.
//
//   - Limb cylinders: bone distances are correct
//     (Thigh→Calf 16.531, Calf→Foot 15.916), but the
//     radius=3 was too tight for the visible mesh
//     thickness. Bumped:
//       SHOULDER: radius 3,4 → 5,5
//       KNEE:     radius 3,3 → 6,6
//       LEGS:     radius 3,2/3 → 6,6
//
// HEAD unchanged: radius 6 sphere matches the legacy
// REALHEAD_HEAD size (g_combat.c:G_BuildHead) and was the
// only region that worked reliably in v0.3.3.
//
// Auto-loaded by mdx_LoadHitsFile from
// characterDef.animationgroup ("animations/human_base.anim"
// → "animations/human_base.hit"). Shared by all 10 vanilla
// ETLegacy classes (Soldier/Medic/Engineer/FieldOps/Cvops
// × Allies/Axis).
//
// 9 distinct impact-points, 10 hit-areas (LEGS has 2:
// left + right calf-foot cylinders).
//
// Bone names: 3DS-Max Biped naming with "Bip01" prefix.
// Quoted because they contain spaces.
//
// Format constraints (verified parser behaviour, see
// docs/HITS_FORMAT.md §3.0 and §3.2):
//   1. TAG and HIT blocks must be SINGLE-LINE — the parser
//      uses COM_ParseExt with allowLineBreaks=qfalse, so it
//      stops at newlines inside a block.
//   2. HIT blocks resolve names via cachetag_cache /
//      mdm_tag_lookup, NOT mdx_bone_lookup. Bone names from
//      the .mdx skeleton must be bridged through TAG blocks
//      first; only TAG block second-tokens hit the bone-name
//      lookup path.
//
// Spec: docs/HITS_FORMAT.md
// Plan: docs/notes/HITBOX_SCALE_ANALYSIS.md (Phase 6.1.3)

// ---- TAG bridges (internal-tag → bone) ----
// Each TAG declares an internal tag that wraps a real
// skeleton bone. mdx_bone_lookup is case-sensitive (strcmp),
// so the bone-name spelling must match the .mdx exactly.
//
// _vg_head applies a `+6.5` offset along the head bone's local
// X axis. The Bip01 Head bone-origin in the 3DS-Max biped
// skeleton sits at the atlas / skull-base — a radius-6 sphere
// centered there lands on the chin/upper-neck in the visible
// mesh, far below the actual skull-cap. v0.4.1 first attempted
// `offset 0 0 6.5` (Z), copying the legacy mdx_head_position
// constant verbatim — but mdx_head_position uses world-frame
// `orientation.axis[2]` (an MDM tag's axis, modeled with `axis[2]
// = up` by convention), whereas mdx_tag_orientation rotates
// interntag offsets by the BONE-LOCAL axis matrix from
// mdx_bone_orientation. For a 3DS-Max biped bone, local +X is
// the bone direction (parent → child), confirmed by
// `mdx_calculate_bone` (g_mdx.c:1402) where parent_dist is
// placed on `tmp[0]` (X). So for Bip01 Head — whose child
// direction is "up the skull" in the rest pose — bone-local +X
// is the world-up direction the offset has to follow. v0.4.1
// shipped with `0 0 6.5` and produced a sphere that wandered to
// the back of the head (top-down view: on the medic-pack
// backpack); v0.4.2 switches to the correct axis. The matching
// offset is hardcoded in cgame's vg_hit_areas[] HEAD entry so
// the wireframe visualisation tracks the real trace position.
//
// The 0.5 forward component that mdx_head_position also applies
// is intentionally omitted — for an isotropic radius-6 sphere
// it has no effect on the hit volume centre.

TAG _vg_head      "Bip01 Head" offset 6.5 0 0
TAG _vg_neck      "Bip01 Neck"
TAG _vg_spine_lo  "Bip01 Spine"
TAG _vg_spine_mid "Bip01 Spine1"
TAG _vg_spine_up  "Bip01 Spine2"
TAG _vg_spine_top "Bip01 Spine3"
TAG _vg_pelvis    "Bip01 Pelvis"
TAG _vg_clav_l    "Bip01 L Clavicle"
TAG _vg_uarm_l    "Bip01 L UpperArm"
TAG _vg_clav_r    "Bip01 R Clavicle"
TAG _vg_uarm_r    "Bip01 R UpperArm"
TAG _vg_thigh_l   "Bip01 L Thigh"
TAG _vg_calf_l    "Bip01 L Calf"
TAG _vg_foot_l    "Bip01 L Foot"
TAG _vg_thigh_r   "Bip01 R Thigh"
TAG _vg_calf_r    "Bip01 R Calf"
TAG _vg_foot_r    "Bip01 R Foot"

// ---- HIT areas (10 blocks, 9 distinct impact-points) ----
// Each line is one HIT block. tokens are: hit_type, then
// 1-2 internal-tag references, then per-tag and per-hit
// modifiers, all on the same line. impactpoint is the
// per-region damage classification used by the multiplier
// table; hit_type is the coarser pain-animation category.

// Head — sphere on the head bone (1 tag, no box → sphere).
HIT head _vg_head radius 6 impactpoint head

// Chest — box Spine1 → Neck (Z ≈ 16.58 units), upper torso.
HIT body _vg_spine_mid _vg_neck scale 9 7 5 scale 9 7 5 impactpoint chest box

// Gut — box Pelvis → Spine2 (Z ≈ 10.53 units), lower torso.
HIT body _vg_pelvis _vg_spine_up scale 9 7 5 scale 9 7 5 impactpoint gut box

// Groin — sphere at the pelvis bone, hip/lower-pelvis area.
HIT body _vg_pelvis radius 7 impactpoint groin

// Left Shoulder — cylinder Clavicle → UpperArm.
HIT arm_L _vg_clav_l _vg_uarm_l radius 5 radius 5 impactpoint shoulder_left

// Right Shoulder — mirror of left.
HIT arm_R _vg_clav_r _vg_uarm_r radius 5 radius 5 impactpoint shoulder_right

// Left Knee — cylinder Thigh → Calf; mid-region = knee joint.
HIT leg_L _vg_thigh_l _vg_calf_l radius 6 radius 6 impactpoint knee_left

// Right Knee — mirror of left.
HIT leg_R _vg_thigh_r _vg_calf_r radius 6 radius 6 impactpoint knee_right

// Left Leg (calf/shin) — cylinder Calf → Foot. Both legs
// share IMPACTPOINT_LEGS — the enum has no L/R split.
HIT leg_L _vg_calf_l _vg_foot_l radius 6 radius 6 impactpoint legs

// Right Leg (calf/shin).
HIT leg_R _vg_calf_r _vg_foot_r radius 6 radius 6 impactpoint legs
